motd-forge (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Alert on recent errors in the system journal (journalctl -p err), shown
    with their age and a hint.
  * Errors and failed units older than 48 hours (alert_max_age_hours) no
    longer raise an alert, so the banner returns to the normal theme rotation.
  * Log text is stripped of terminal control characters before display.

 -- motd-forge maintainers <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0000

motd-forge (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the libc6 dependency: require glibc 2.34 (Debian 12+) instead of the
    2.39 that dpkg-shlibdeps derived from two optional symbols.

 -- motd-forge maintainers <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000

motd-forge (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rewrite in Rust: a single self-contained binary, no Python, no
    third-party crates. Themes are built in; custom themes still load from
    ~/.config/motd-forge/themes and /usr/share/motd-forge/themes.
  * Architecture is now "any" (published for amd64).

 -- motd-forge maintainers <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

motd-forge (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.

